Literature check -- single edge crack of depth h in a half plane,
remote tension sigma0:  K = F * sigma0 sqrt(pi h) with F = 1.1215.
Here the crack is fully open (faces traction free after full relaxation),
so the same universal F = 1.1215 should apply.

Singular-basis equilibrium solve (w = hats + C/sqrt(1-zeta)):
  N= 200  singular amplitude C = -0.1466   residual(rel) = 3.484e-12
  N= 400  singular amplitude C = -0.1131   residual(rel) = 1.553e-11
  (a sizeable C shows the equilibrium solution does carry a sqrt tip density,
   i.e. the boundary becomes crack-like -> K_inf = 1.1215 sigma0 sqrt(pi h).)
